  "content": {
    "id": "v2-50cd33f8a-practice-slot-2-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": null,
    "prompt": "Find the tangent and normal to the curve $y=x(2x-3)^3$ at the point $A(1,-1)$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "Tangent: $y=5x-6$.\n\nNormal: $y=-\\dfrac{x}{5}-\\dfrac45$.",
      "worked": "Let $u=x$ and $v=(2x-3)^3$. Then $u'=1$ and $v'=6(2x-3)^2$.\n$$\\begin{align*}y'&=u'v+uv'\\\\&=(2x-3)^3+6x(2x-3)^2\\\\&=(2x-3)^2[(2x-3)+6x]\\\\&=(2x-3)^2(8x-3).\\end{align*}$$\nAt $x=1$,\n$$m_T=(-1)^2(5)=5.$$\nHence $m_N=-\\dfrac15$.\n\nTangent:\n$$\\begin{align*}y+1&=5(x-1)\\\\y&=5x-6.\\end{align*}$$\nNormal:\n$$\\begin{align*}y+1&=-\\frac15(x-1)\\\\y&=-\\frac{x}{5}-\\frac45.\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": null
  },
